    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0720" n="706" xml:id="pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/8–1144</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kapustin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-11">August 11,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Referring to my letter
                    of July 24<anchor n="72" xml:id="d414-f1"/> I have the honor to inform you
                    additionally of the full composition of the delegation of the U.S.S.R.,
                    appointed by the Government of the U.S.S.R. for participation in the forthcoming
                    informal discussions on the questions of establishment of an international
                    organization of security.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman of the Delegation</hi>, Andrei Andreyevich
                            Gromyko<anchor n="73" xml:id="d414-f2"/>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Deputy-Chairman</hi>, Arkadi Alexandrovich
                            Sobolev<anchor n="74" xml:id="d414-f3"/>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Members of the Delegation:</hi>
                        <list>
                            <item>Semen Konstantinovich Zarapkin<anchor n="75" xml:id="d414-f4"/>
                            </item>
                            <item>Maj. General Nikolai Vassilievich Slavin<anchor n="76"
                                    xml:id="d414-f5"/>
                            </item>
                            <item>Rear Admiral Konstantin Konstantinovich Rodionov<anchor n="77"
                                    xml:id="d414-f6"/>
                            </item>
                            <item>Professor Sergei Alexandrovich Golunsky</item>
                            <item>Professor Sergei Borisovich Krylov<anchor n="78" xml:id="d414-f7"
                                />
                            </item>
                            <item>Grigori Georgievich Dolbin<anchor n="79" xml:id="d414-f8"/>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Delegation</hi>, Mikhail
                        Mikhailovich Yunin</item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary-interpreter</hi>, Valentin Mikhailovich
                            Berezhkov<anchor n="80" xml:id="d414-f9"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kapustin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="72" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f2" n="73" xml:id="d414-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f3" n="74" xml:id="d414-f3-content">
                <p>Minister Counselor of Embassy in the United Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f4" n="75" xml:id="d414-f4-content">
                <p>Chief of the American section of the Soviet Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f5" n="76" xml:id="d414-f5-content">
                <p>Member of the Soviet General Staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f6" n="77" xml:id="d414-f6-content">
                <p>Chief of the Administrative Division of the Navy Commissariat.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f7" n="78" xml:id="d414-f7-content">
                <p>Member of the Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f8" n="79" xml:id="d414-f8-content">
                <p>Professor of international law at Moscow University.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f9" n="80" xml:id="d414-f9-content"> Counselor, Soviet Foreign
                Office. <p>Press Officer Feodor T. Orekhov was also included in the personnel list
                    in <hi rendition="#italic">Postwar Foreign Policy Preparation</hi>, p. 304.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
